addrmap hi3516ev300 {
    name = "hi3516ev300 registers";
    desc = "
        ## Status

        Register map of the Hi3516E V300 (Cortex-A7 IP camera SoC, DDR at 0x40000000). Audited block by block on 2026-11-14 against the Hi3516E V300 data sheet, Issue 00B06 (2019-05-15, dl/Hi3516EV300-Datasheet.pdf): the blocks named ds_*.rdl were regenerated from the data sheet tables (PROVEN: offsets, names, bit ranges, access types, reset values exact; descriptions sampled only) and replaced the earlier vendor-code derived blocks (second pass 2026-11-15: array registers of the DDRC AXI, VICAP, MIPI RX and SPACC blocks now have their instance counts from the data sheet variable tables, the FE PHY MII registers (Table 5-8) are modelled in ds_fephy.rdl, USB PHY ANA_CFG0/ANA_CFG4 carry the data sheet fields, RSA MEM_EMA_CFG added, split field names and page-break losses in CRG/LSADC/FMC/MIPI RX/SPACC repaired); registers the old map knew from vendor code but the data sheet does not tabulate were kept in CRG and SYS_CTRL, marked INFERRED. Blocks the data sheet has no register chapter for (ISP, VIPROC, VGS, GZIP, IVE, VPSS, VEDU, JPGE, TDE, IO config banks, SYSCNT, DDRT; the USB PHY has only ANA_CFG0 and ANA_CFG4; the data sheet interrupt table (Table 3-6) lists no register) and the shared common blocks that match the data sheet (FEMAC, I2C, UART, SPI, PL061 GPIO, SP804 timers, SP805 watchdog, PWM, RSA, SPI RTC) keep their earlier vendor-derived or cross-checked layout; the audit results per block are in docs/rdl-campaign/audit-status.csv and docs/rdl-campaign/hi3516ev300-audit.md of the hi3520d-nvr workspace. Nothing was read from an EV300.

        ## Addresses (vendor device tree, vendor U-Boot and sys.ko; IRQ = GIC SPI number, equal to the interrupt bit of data sheet Table 3-6 minus 32: every number in this table was checked against that table on 2026-11-15)

        | Start Address | Block | IRQ | Documented Here |
        |---------------|-------|-----|-----------------|
        | 0x04010000    | on-chip SRAM 64 KB (U-Boot RAM_START_ADRS 0x04010500) | - | &#10060; |
        | 0x10000000    | FMC control (memory window 0x14000000, 16 MB) | 32 (data sheet Table 3-6, bit 64) | &#9989; |
        | 0x10010000    | eMMC / SDIO0 (SDHCI + vendor regs) | 30 | &#9989; |
        | 0x10020000    | SDIO1 (SDHCI + vendor regs) | 31 | &#9989; |
        | 0x10030000    | USB2 DWC3 (high-speed, host) | 39 | &#9989; (vendor glue registers only) |
        | 0x10040000    | FEMAC (internal FE PHY, MDIO 0x10041100, GLB 0x10041300) | 33 (FE PHY interrupt: 59) | &#9989; |
        | 0x10048000    | FE PHY MII registers (placeholder instance: reached through MDIO, not memory mapped; data sheet Table 5-8) | - | &#9989; |
        | 0x10050000    | CIPHER (SPACC layout, version register 0x308 = 0x02018121) | 34 | &#9989; |
        | 0x10060000    | KLAD | - | &#9989; |
        | 0x10070000    | RSA | - | &#9989; |
        | 0x10080000    | TRNG (registers at +0x200) | - | &#9989; |
        | 0x10090000    | OTP controller (user interface) | - | &#9989; |
        | 0x100A0000    | reserved in the data sheet (the vendor tree names it the OTP user shadow) | - | &#10060; |
        | 0x100B0000    | EDMAC hiedmacv310 (4 channels) | 38 | &#9989; |
        | 0x100C0000    | IO config bank ahb | - | &#9989; |
        | 0x100D0000    | USB2 PHY (hixvp) | - | &#9989; |
        | 0x100E0000    | AIAO | 42 | &#9989; |
        | 0x100F0000    | ACODEC | - | &#9989; |
        | 0x10301000    | GIC distributor (cpu interface 0x10302000) | - | &#10060; |
        | 0x11000000    | VI capture (2 MB) | 43 | &#9989; (subset) |
        | 0x11200000    | VI process (VIPROC) | 44 | &#9989; (subset) |
        | 0x11220000    | ISP (128 KB) | 43 | &#10060; |
        | 0x11240000    | MIPI RX (one controller) | 45 | &#9989; (EV200 block) |
        | 0x11280000    | VO | 40 / 41 (hifb) | &#9989; (heuristic map) |
        | 0x112C0000    | IO config bank vio | - | &#9989; |
        | 0x11300000    | VGS | 49 | &#10060; |
        | 0x11310000    | GZIP | 50 | &#9989; |
        | 0x11320000    | IVE | 51 | &#9989; |
        | 0x11330000    | DDRT (no register table in the data sheet; IRQ bit 85 = SPI 53, DDR_ERR SPI 54) | 53 | &#10060; |
        | 0x11400000    | VPSS | 46 | &#9989; (subset) |
        | 0x11410000    | VEDU | 47 | &#9989; (subset) |
        | 0x11420000    | JPGE | 48 | &#9989; (subset) |
        | 0x12000000    | Timers 0/1 (SP804) | 5 | &#9989; |
        | 0x12001000    | Timers 2/3 (SP804) | 6 | &#9989; |
        | 0x12010000    | CRG | - | &#9989; |
        | 0x12020000    | SYS_CTRL | - | &#9989; |
        | 0x12028000    | MISC_CTRL | - | &#9989; |
        | 0x12030000    | WDG | 2 | &#9989; |
        | 0x12040000    | UART0 / 1 / 2 (PL011, stride 0x1000) | 7 / 8 / 9 | &#9989; |
        | 0x12050000    | SYSCNT (50 MHz generic counter) | - | &#10060; |
        | 0x12060000    | I2C0 / 1 / 2 (hibvt, stride 0x1000) | 11 / 12 / 13 (data sheet bits 43-45) | &#9989; |
        | 0x12070000    | SPI0 / SPI1 (PL022) | 14 / 15 | &#9989; |
        | 0x12080000    | PWM (4 channels, stride 0x20) | - | &#9989; |
        | 0x120A0000    | LSADC (2 channels) | 4 | &#9989; |
        | 0x120B0000    | GPIO0..9 (PL061, stride 0x1000) | 16..25 | &#9989; |
        | 0x120C0000    | IO config bank core | - | &#9989; |
        | 0x120D0000    | DDR AXI (DMC at 0x120D8000, PHY at 0x120DC000) | - | &#9989; (EV200 blocks, see note) |
        | 0x120E0000    | RTC (SPI bridge) | 0 | &#9989; |
        | 0x120F0000    | PMC | - | &#9989; |

        <!-- overview:begin -->

        ### Diagrams

        ![Logic block diagram](assets/diagrams/hi3516ev300-logic.svg)

        ![Register blocks by function](assets/diagrams/hi3516ev300-blocks.svg)

        ![Clock tree](assets/diagrams/hi3516ev300-clocks.svg)

        ![Boot flow](assets/diagrams/hi3516ev300-boot.svg)

        ![Video pipeline](assets/diagrams/hi3516ev300-video.svg)

        ![Reset tree](assets/diagrams/hi3516ev300-resets.svg)

        ![Storage, USB and Ethernet paths](assets/diagrams/hi3516ev300-io.svg)

        ![DMA request lines](assets/diagrams/hi3516ev300-dma.svg)

        ![Bus masters and DDR QoS groups](assets/diagrams/hi3516ev300-busqos.svg)

        ![Power domains](assets/diagrams/hi3516ev300-power.svg)

        ### Variants and key specifications (data sheet chapter 1; brief data sheets for the siblings)

        The register map of this folder covers the Hi3516E V300. The family siblings with brief data sheets only are the Hi3516E V200 and the Hi3518E V300 (folder hi3516ev200); the vendor SDK also names a Hi3516D V200 (INFERRED sibling, no data sheet). The chip ID register (SYS_CTRL 0xEE0) reads 0x3516E300 here (vendor module value, not hardware-read).

        | | Hi3516E V300 (this chip) | Hi3516E V200 (brief sheet) | Hi3518E V300 (brief sheet) |
        |---|---|---|---|
        | CPU | Cortex-A7 up to 900 MHz, NEON + FPU, 32 KB I + 32 KB D L1, 128 KB L2, one core | same | same |
        | DDR | built-in 1 Gbit DDR3L, 16-bit, 1.35 V | built-in 512 Mbit DDR2, 16-bit, 1.8 V | built-in 512 Mbit DDR2, 16-bit |
        | Video encode | H.264 BP/MP/HP, H.265 MP, MJPEG/JPEG; up to 2688 x 1520 or 2592 x 1944; 2048 x 1536@30 + 720 x 576@30, 2688 x 1520@15 + 720 x 576@15; JPEG 4M@5 / 5M@5; 8 ROIs; up to 60 Mbit/s | same codecs; up to 2304 x 1296; 2048 x 1536@20, 1920 x 1080@30; JPEG 3M@5 | same as V200 |
        | Video input | 8/10/12-bit Bayer DC timing, BT.1120, MIPI, LVDS / sub-LVDS, HiSPi; up to 2688 x 1520 | same interfaces; up to 2304 x 1296 | same as V200 |
        | Video output | 6/8/16-bit LCD, BT.656 / BT.1120 | 6/8-bit LCD, BT.656 / BT.1120 | 6/8-bit LCD, BT.656 |
        | Audio | integrated codec 16-bit, 2-channel MIC / line-in, 2-channel line-out, I2S | mono MIC / line-in, mono line-out, I2S | dual MIC / line-in, mono line-out, I2S |
        | Storage and network | SPI NOR (256 MB max), SPI NAND (1 GB max), eMMC 5.0 4/8-bit; 2 x SDIO 2.0; USB 2.0 host / device; FE PHY with TSO | NOR, NAND, eMMC 4.5 4-bit; 1 x SDIO 2.0 + 1 x SD 2.0; USB 2.0; FE PHY with TSO | same as V200 |
        | Peripherals | RTC, POR, 4-channel LSADC, 3 UART, I2C, SPI, GPIO, 4 PWM, PMC standby unit | RTC, POR, 2-channel LSADC, 3 UART, I2C, SPI, GPIO, 4 PWM | same as V200 |
        | Security | AES, RSA, SHA1/SHA256/HMAC, 32 kbit OTP, TRNG, secure boot | same | same |
        | Package | TFBGA 12 x 13.3 mm, 279 balls, 0.65 mm pitch | QFN 9 x 9 mm, 88 pins, 0.35 mm pitch | QFN 9 x 9 mm, 88 pins |
        | Power | core 0.9 V, I/O 3.3 V, DDR3L 1.35 V; 1 W typical (3M30 / 4M15) | core 0.9 V, I/O 3.3 V, SDRAM 1.8 V; 700 mW typical (1080P30 / 3M20) | same as V200 |

        Common to all three: ISP with 3A, WDR (sensor built-in, 2F line / frame), DPC, LSC, LDC, local tone mapping, BayerNR + 3DNR, DIS, 4 x 4 RGB-IR; VPSS with VGS (3DNR, scaling 1/15x to 16x, rotation, mirror, 8-region OSD); IVE; audio 3A in software. The SDK is a LiteOS / Linux 4.9 package.

        ### Boot (data sheet 1.4)

        The BOOTROM runs after reset release. BOOT_SEL1 (power-on latch of pin LCD_CLK) and BOOT_SEL0 (latch of pin LCD_DE) are readable in SYS_CTRL SYSSTAT[5:4]; UPDATE_MODE is the level of GPIO0_0 at start (0 = key pressed).

        | UPDATE_MODE | BOOT_SEL1 | BOOT_SEL0 | Mode |
        |---|---|---|---|
        | 1 | 0 | 0 | boot from SPI NOR or SPI NAND |
        | 1 | 0 | 1 | boot from eMMC |
        | 1 | 1 | 0 | serial-port burn of SPI NOR / NAND images |
        | 1 | 1 | 1 | serial-port burn of eMMC images |
        | 0 | X | 0 | upgrade SPI NOR / NAND from SD card (SDIO0 only) or USB |
        | 0 | X | 1 | upgrade eMMC from SD card (not possible when booting from eMMC) or USB |

        Secure boot: SYSSTAT[31] (from the OTP secure-boot flag) selects signature verification of U-Boot.

        ### DMA request lines (data sheet 3.6.3.1, Table 3-8)

        One DMAC with four channels (see the DMAC block above); memory-to-memory transfers use no request line. The request line IDs are:

        | ID | Peripheral | ID | Peripheral | ID | Peripheral |
        |---|---|---|---|---|---|
        | 0 | I2C0 RX | 16 | UART0 RX | 26 | SPI0 RX |
        | 1 | I2C0 TX | 17 | UART0 TX | 27 | SPI0 TX |
        | 2 | I2C1 RX | 18 | UART1 RX | 28 | SPI1 RX |
        | 3 | I2C1 TX | 19 | UART1 TX | 29 | SPI1 TX |
        | 4 | I2C2 RX | 20 | UART2 RX | 6-15, 22-25, 30-31 | reserved |
        | 5 | I2C2 TX | 21 | UART2 TX | | |

        ### Pinmux function summary (VENDOR-DERIVED, INFERRED)

        The data sheet has no pin chapter (pins are in a separate pinout document, not in the workspace). The three pad banks (IO config ahb 0x100C0000, core 0x120C0000, vio 0x112C0000) hold one 32-bit word per pad, offset / 4 = pad index. Field layout [3:0] function, [7:4] drive, [8] pull-up, [9] pull-down, [10] slew is INFERRED from U-Boot pad code. Functions used by the vendor pinmux tables (sys_config):

        | Function | Bank and pad offsets | Note |
        |---|---|---|
        | VI (MIPI / raw / BT.656), sensor input | vio 0x00 - 0x64 | pad function 0 = GPIO / MIPI mode, 2 / 3 = VI CMOS (vendor values) |
        | Sensor clock and reset | vio 0x28, 0x2C | function 1 (sensor clock out) |
        | I2C0 | vio 0x30, 0x34 | |
        | I2C2 | vio 0x38, 0x3C | |
        | I2C1 | ahb 0x0C, 0x10 | |
        | SPI0 | vio 0x9C, 0xA0, 0xA4 | |
        | SPI1 | ahb 0x84 - 0x90 | |
        | VO: BT.1120 / BT.656 / LCD | vio 0x48 - 0x94 | |
        | I2S | core 0x10 - 0x20 | |
        | LSADC | core 0x00, 0x04 | |
        | IR input | ahb 0x08 | |
        | PWM3 / GPIO9_1 | ahb 0xA0 | |
        | eMMC | ahb 0x14 - 0x5C | |
        | SDIO0 | ahb 0x40 - 0x54 | |

        ### Power and reset domains (data sheet 2.5.3, 3.1, 3.10)

        * Always-on area: PMC (0x120F0000) and the RTC. The PMC runs from the 32.768 kHz RTC clock and needs the RTC crystal and AVDD_BAT. It controls the external supply sequencer (PWR_SEQ) that powers the rest of the chip on and off; features: wakeup polarity, power-on / off timing, RTC timed power-on, forced power-on by holding PWR_BUTTON for 10.2 s. Pins PWR_WAKEUP, PWR_STARTUP, PWR_BUTTON and PWR_RSTN; without the PMC, PWR_RSTN gets an RC reset and the others float.
        * Supply rails (Table 2-13): AVDD33_PLL, AVDD33_USB2, AVDD33_AC, AVDD33_FE 3.3 V; AVDD_BAT 1.6 - 3.6 V; DVDD33 (JTAG / LSADC / LCD); DVDD3318_PC, DVDD3318_SENSOR, DVDD3318_FLASH (SFC / SDIO0 / PWM / UART0 / SYS), DVDD3318_VIVO (LCD) each 1.8 or 3.3 V; AVDD3318_MIPIRX 1.8 V (3.3 V when the MIPI pads are single-ended); VDDIO_DDR 1.35 V; core 0.9 V.
        * Low-power measures: clock gating and frequency scaling, module low-power control, DDR self-refresh / low-power control, adaptive voltage scaling.
        * Reset: POR (internal, low pulse over 12 XIN cycles), watchdog reset and the global soft reset (SC_SYSRES, protected by SC_LOCKEN) are system resets; every block has its own soft-reset bit in the CRG. After a global soft reset request the circuit stays reset at least 360 system clocks and no second request may come within that time; per-block resets are held until software clears the bit.

        ### Clock selections (data sheet Table 3-2)

        | Module | Default | Selectable |
        |---|---|---|
        | A7 | 24 MHz | 24, 600, 900 MHz |
        | DDR | 24 MHz | 24, 300, 450 MHz |
        | SYSAXI / SYSCFG / SYSAPB | 24 MHz | 200 / 100 / 50 MHz |
        | VPSS, VIPROC | 257 MHz | 75, 100, 150, 200, 257 MHz |
        | VICAP / MIPI pixel | 360 MHz | 75, 100, 150, 200, 257, 300 (offline only), 360 (offline only) MHz |
        | IVE | 450 MHz | 100, 300, 360, 450 MHz |
        | FMC | 24 MHz | 24, 100, 150, 200, 300 and 360 (both DDR mode only) MHz |
        | eMMC / SDIO0 | 100 kHz | 100 kHz, 400 kHz, 25, 50 MHz; 90, 112.5, 150 MHz (eMMC mode only) |
        | SDIO1 | 100 kHz | 100 kHz, 400 kHz, 25, 50 MHz |

        PLL formula (Table 3-4): FOUTVCO = 24 MHz x (fbdiv + frac / 2^24) / refdiv, valid between 800 MHz and 3.2 GHz; FOUTPOSTDIV = FOUTVCO / (pstdiv1 x pstdiv2), pstdiv1 >= pstdiv2. Reconfigure only after switching the consumers to a non-PLL clock, then wait 0.1 ms and poll the lock bits (PERI_CRG_PLL122).

        ### Bus matrix

        The data sheet does not tabulate the interconnect. What exists is the DDR QoS group per master (3 bits, MISC_CTRL32-34 write and MISC_CTRL36-38 read, masters: CPU, DMAC, SPACC, FMC, USB, SDIO0, SDIO1, ETH, VDP, VICAP, VIPROC, JPGE, VEDU, VPSS, IVE / DDRT, VGS / GZIP, AIAO) and the media bus port priorities (MISC_CTRL28: VPSS port 0, VEDU port 1, JPGE port 2). See the bus diagram above. Which master sits on which DDRC AXI port is not stated.

        ### Clock-gate and reset map (generated from the CRG registers)

        | Offset | Register | Description | Gate / reset fields |
